// Regla Sigma: proc_creation_win_cmd_sticky_keys_replace.yml
// ID Sigma: 1070db9a-3e5d-412e-8e7b-7183b616e1b3
// Título: Persistence Via Sticky Key Backdoor
// Descripción: By replacing the sticky keys executable with the local admins CMD executable, an attacker is able to access a privileged windows console session without authenticating to the system.
When the sticky keys are "activated" the privilleged shell is launched.

// Aplica a: Producto: windows | Categoría: process_creation
// Producto: windows
// Categoría: process_creation
// Servicio: 
// Nivel: critical
// Pipeline: microsoft_xdr
// Ruta original: C:\SigmaLab\sigma\rules\windows\process_creation\proc_creation_win_cmd_sticky_keys_replace.yml
// Requiere validación en el entorno de destino.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "copy " and ProcessCommandLine contains "/y " and ProcessCommandLine contains "C:\\windows\\system32\\cmd.exe C:\\windows\\system32\\sethc.exe"
